# Source of truth for the protobuf-5 all-features umbrella CI lock
# (Serverless env 5 / classic DBR 17.3–18, full feature set).
# Covers: light_env5_all, light_dbr17_all, light_dbr18_all — all alias
# geobrix[light_dbr17_all], the canonical pb5 all-features extra.
#
# Regenerate (from python/geobrix/):
#   uv pip compile --generate-hashes --python-version 3.12 \
#       --output-file requirements-light-env5-all-ci.txt requirements-light-env5-all-ci.in
#
# This .in uses a local-package-with-extra reference so uv expands [light_env5_all]
# directly from pyproject.toml. The [light_env5_all] extra pulls
# [light_dbr17]+[stac]+[vizx] (protobuf-5 / mapbox-vector-tile<2.2).
# ([overture] is an opt-in extra outside the _all umbrellas.)
# Protobuf-6 all-features twin: see requirements-light-env6-all-ci.in.
#
# Note: CI resolves without Serverless grpcio-status constraints; the protobuf version
# in this lock (5.x) reflects the [light_dbr17] cap on mapbox-vector-tile, NOT a CI
# grpcio constraint. The real runtime protobuf is set at cluster install time.

# Local package — expands geobrix[light_env5_all] from pyproject.toml
.[light_env5_all]

# pyspark is NOT a geobrix base dependency (Databricks provides it on every supported
# runtime; see pyproject.toml). This lock is for local/manual verification off-cluster,
# so pin it explicitly — same floor the base dependency used to carry.
pyspark>=4.0.0

# pillow is resolved through [vizx] (matplotlib, scikit-image, imageio, contextily) and certifi
# through requests and httpx2; the floors keep a regenerated lock at the security-patched
# releases. CI-only: the extras in pyproject.toml are unchanged, and pip leaves the runtime's own
# pillow and certifi in place.
pillow>=13.0.0
certifi>=2026.10.19
